xperience and health.Since the question asks for the "most likely", even if he\'s over 60, his other factors might make him the best choice.\n\nOption D\'s Lao Ma lacks earthquake experience, so he\'s excluded.\n\nOption A is excluded due to age.\n\nSo between B and C:.\n\nIf C\'s experience counts, then he\'s okay.But B has more experience and is a man in good health (even if not currently in medical work, but maybe the "currently" is key here.Since he retired, he\'s not currently engaged, so only the "in good health" applies.So he is a man in good health, which makes him more likely.\n\nC is a man (assuming Xiao Li is male), but he\'s not in medical work, and his health isn\'t mentioned.His experience might be minimal.So B\'s experience is stronger.\n\nTherefore, B is the best candidate despite being over 60 because of his experience and health.The problem says "over 60" are least likely, but that doesn\'t mean they can\'t be selected if they have other strengths.Since the question asks for the most likely, B might still be the answer.\n\nWait, but the problem says "those who are least likely to be recruited are those under the age of 20, over 60, or people who have no experience.." So being over 60 makes someone least likely, but if they have other positive traits, they might still be selected.The question is which is "most likely".\n\nComparing B and C again:.\n\nB has:.\n\n- Over 60 (negative).\n- Experience: lots (positive).The answer is not B.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
