      "text": " B does not reflect related marketing because it's promoting the same product through an experience rather than integrating different products.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is **B**. \n\n**Explanation:**  \nThe definition of related marketing emphasizes integrating resources to highlight relevance between products or brands, guiding customers toward multiple related items.  \n\n- **Option A** displays complementary products (sunscreen, sunglasses) near swimsuits, leveraging their functional connection.  \n- **Option C** uses customer data to cross-sell age-appropriate products, aligning with tailored recommendations.  \n- **Option D** extends a popular design to related product styles (V-neck, vertical-collar), diversifying the core offering.  \n\n**Option B**, however, focuses on enhancing the experience of the *same product* (TVs) through an experiential setup. It does not integrate or cross-promote additional products or brands, thus failing to meet the criteria of \"related marketing\" as defined.  \n\n**Answer:** B",
