ble2 (5-1 difference).Suppose she has5 points.To get5, she could have two wins (4) and one tie (1), totaling5.Her opponent has1 point (from one tie and two losses).Thus, she tied one game.\n\nAlternatively, if she has1, but then her opponent has5.\n\nSince Zhang is paired with Lu Wei, and the pair has5-1.If Zhang has5 and Lu has1, then Zhang has two wins and one tie (5=2+2+1), so she tied once.\n\nThus, Zhang could have tied.\n\nYang Hong (option B) is at table4 with difference3-3.They must have tied all three games (each gets1 per game, totaling3 each).Thus, she tied all three.\n\nBut condition (3) says Zhao Hu\'s pair has no ties.If Yang is at4 with Zhao, then they tied all games, violating condition (3).But if the boy at4 is not Zhao, like Fan, then their tie is allowed.\n\nShi Lin (option A): If she is at table1 with6 points, she couldn\'t have tied any games.\n\nSo possible answers are B, C, or D.\n\nBut need to check constraints:\n\nIf Yang Hong (B) tied all three games at table4, then her opponent must have also tied all three.If the opponent is Fan (at table4), then Fan\'s points would be3, but he must be leading.Contradiction.\n\nIf the opponent is Zhao, then Zhao\'s points are3, but condition (3) says Zhao\'s points are not ahead and no ties.Ties are present, so invalid.\n\nThus, Yang cannot be the answer.\n\nZhang Fang (C): If she has5 points with one tie, that\'s possible.\n\nFan (D): If he has two ties and a win, that\'s possible.\n\nNow, condition (3) says Zhao\'s pair has no ties.If Zhao is at table3 with Wang Yu, and their scores are4-2 with no ties, then that\'s okay.\n\nSo between C and D.In this scenario, it is clear that Fan Yong did not make a tie with his opponent in the first three rounds, contrary to initial assumptions. Zhang Fang is also not a candidate for tying a game in this context, given the constraints provided.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 15%|#5        | 90/600 [1:01:31<2:58:24, 20.99s/it]
