      "text": " C\n</think>\n\nThe context emphasizes that Chinese literati have historically dominated the discourse on painting, shaping evaluations from their own perspective and marginalizing non-literati artists. \n\n**Analysis of options:**  \n- **A** discusses a lag between appreciation and creative levels, which the text does not address.  \n- **B** incorrectly states that \"talented literati and artists\" were overlooked, whereas the text specifies *non-literati* artists were neglected.  \n- **C** directly aligns with the text\u2019s claim that literati \"have dominated the discussion space of painting for a long time\" in theory.  \n- **D** mentions a \"difference of interest\" between literati and non-literati, which is not explicitly stated; the focus is on dominance and bias, not differing interests.  \n\n**Answer:** C) The literati have been in a strong position in the field of Chinese painting theory for a long time.",
