n this inference, the missing link is establishing that sodium salts *require liquid water* to exist. \n\n- **Option D** directly bridges the premise (sodium salts) and the conclusion (liquid water). If sodium salts can only exist in the presence of liquid water, their detection becomes strong evidence for liquid water, which is the foundational claim in the speculation.  \n- Other options address tangential points:  \n  - **A** ties eruptions to an underground sea but does not directly connect sodium salts to liquid water.  \n  - **B** specifies that liquid water must form an underground sea but does not validate the sodium salts \u2192 liquid water relationship.  \n  - **C** focuses on eruptions enabling sodium salt detection, which is irrelevant since sodium salts are already observed.  \n\nThus, **D** most effectively strengthens the core logical leap from sodium salts to liquid water.",
