messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn an exam, there are three questions about tourist attractions in Beijing, requiring candidates to choose the name of a scenic spot as the only answer to each question. The answers of six candidates to the above three questions are as follows: the first candidate: Temple of Heaven, Temple of Heaven, Tiananmen Square; the second candidate: Tiananmen Square, Tiananmen Square; the third candidate: the Forbidden City, the Forbidden City; the fourth candidate: the Temple of Heaven, Tiananmen Square; the fifth candidate: Tiananmen Square, the Forbidden City; the sixth candidate: the Forbidden City, Tiananmen Square, the Forbidden City. The examination results show that each examinee has answered at least one of the questions correctly.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above statement, which of the following options is the order of answers to these three questions?\n# Options:\nA) Temple of heaven, imperial palace, temple of heaven\nB) The imperial palace, tiananmen square, tiananmen square\nC) Tiananmen square, the imperial palace, the temple of heaven\nD) Temple of heaven, temple of heaven, imperial palace', '<think>\nOkay, let\'s tackle this problem step by step.So, we have an exam with three questions about Beijing\'s tourist attractions, and each question has one correct scenic spot answer.There are six candidates who answered the three questions, each giving their own set of answers.The key point is that each candidate got at least one question right.Our job is to figure out the correct answer order from the options given.\n\nFirst, I need to list out each candidate\'s answers clearly.Let me note them down:.\n\n1.Candidate 1: Temple of Heaven (all three answers?), wait, wait, hold on.Wait, the problem says each question requires a single answer, so each candidate has three answers,