inin.\n\nThe context already mentions \"new breakthroughs in antimalarial mechanism research, causes of drug resistance, adjustment of treatment and other aspects.\" So the causes are part of the breakthroughs. A new breakthrough (A) would be in the same field but not mentioned yet. So the next part might introduce that, making it possible. Alternatively, the \"new breakthrough\" is redundant since it's part of the existing ones.\n\nAlternatively, since the context says they made breakthroughs in causes of resistance, then the next part would explain the cause (D) and not introduce a new breakthrough (A), so A is less likely.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A.\n\nBut now I'm confused between A and D. If D's cause is already mentioned as part of the breakthroughs, then the next part would elaborate on that cause, so D is likely to be introduced next. So the least likely is A.\n\nWait, the question is which is least likely to be introduced next. So the answer is A.\n\nAlternatively, the answer is D, but I think I'm overcomplicating. I'll go with option C as the least likely because the contribution of TCM may not be a direct topic following the mentioned points, but the recognition by WHO is mentioned, so it's likely. Thus, the answer must be another option.\n\nWait, the context says \"going out of scientific research works in traditional Chinese medicine hospitals\" which might mean that TCM research is being utilized or disseminated, which would contribute to the world, so C is covered.\n\nTherefore, the only one left is A. The new breakthrough in drug resistance research is part of the existing breakthroughs, so the next part would not introduce a new one. Hence, A is the least likely.\n\nFinal Answer: A\n\nWait, but I'm not sure. Alternatively, the answer is D because the cause is already mentioned.\n\nWait, the question is asking which is least likely to be introduced next. If the next part is going to explain the causes (D) as part of the breakthroughs, then D is li