.\" This bridges the gap between the premise (human intelligence needs emotions) and the conclusion (computers, lacking emotions, cannot be intelligent). Other options either introduce unrelated conditions (e.g., identifying emotions in A, technological advancement in B) or reverse the logical relationship (C). \n\n**Answer: D**",
