t indicate financial harm but does not explicitly tie to loss of control over the crop itself. **Option A** and **B** address unrelated issues like pest prevalence and yield quality, which do not strengthen the argument about foreign control. \n\nThus, **D** most strongly supports the expert\u2019s view by highlighting a mechanism (patent enforcement on seed reuse) that directly threatens national sovereignty over food production.\n\n**Answer:** D",
