detergents contain much lower amounts of surfactants. Since surfactants are known to harm aquatic life, lower amounts in eco-friendly detergents directly provide a reason to believe they are less damaging, weakening the argument.\n- **Option D**: Suggests eco-friendly detergents are less effective, requiring more use. This could increase environmental damage, strengthening the argument instead.\n\n**Conclusion**: Option C provides a valid reason to believe ecologically friendly detergents are less harmful due to reduced surfactants, directly weakening the original argument.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
