messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn the process of accompanying their children, many parents will encounter the problem of their children lying or concealing the truth. Lying is almost what many parents are most worried about. Their children's bad behavior is even more frightening and angry than their children's poor academic performance.If we say that many parents have not solved the problem of their children lying well, at least most of them should pay attention to it, while the problem of children concealing their own situation from their parents is not only worse solved, but also not given enough attention.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is true of the original text?\n# Options:\nA) Parents think that children's failure to report information is more worrying than lying\nB) Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem\nC) Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying\nD) Children's behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents", '<think>\nOkay, let\'s tackle this question.First, I need to read the context carefully and then look at the options to see which one is correct based on the information given.\n\nThe context talks about parents dealing with their children lying or hiding the truth.It says that lying is something many parents are most worried about, and that their children\'s bad behavior is even more frightening and angry than poor academic performance.Then it mentions that while many parents haven\'t solved the lying problem well, at least most pay attention to it.However, the problem of children concealing their situation is not only worse solved but also not given enough attention.\n\nThe question asks which of the options is true according to the original text.Let\'s go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: Parents think that children\'s failure to report information is more worrying than lying.The text says that lying is what parents are most worried about.The concealing part is not as much addressed, but the worry is stated to be higher for lying.So maybe A is incorrect because the text says lying is the main worry, and concealing isn\'t as much focused on, but the question is about what parents think.Wait, the text says "their children\'s bad behavior is even more frightening and angry than their children\'s poor academic performance."Hmm, maybe the bad behavior (which could include lying?)is worse than poor grades, but the problem of concealing is not as addressed.The first sentence says lying is what parents are most worried about.So A says concealing is more worrying than lying, which contradicts the text.So A is wrong.\n\nOption B: Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem.The text says lying is "almost what many parents are most worried about."The wording here is a bit tricky."Most worried about" might not equate to "most unforgivable moral problem."The text doesn\'t explicitly state that it\'s the most unforgivable, just that it\'s a major concern.So B might be stretching the text\'s claims.Maybe not the correct answer.\n\nOption C: Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying.The text says "if we say that many parents have not solved the problem.. at least most of them should pay attention to it."Wait, the wording here is a bit confusing.The original says that many haven\'t solved it well, but most pay attention.So "pay attention to it" doesn\'t mean they are willing to solve it.Maybe they are aware but not actively working on it.The option C says "more than willing," which might not be supported.The text doesn\'t say they are eager, just that they pay attention.So C might be incorrect.\n\nOption D: Children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents.The text states that the problem of concealing is "not only worse solved, but also not given enough attention."So "not given enough attention" means it hasn\'t attracted enough attention, but does that mean it hasn\'t attracted any?The wording in D is "has not attracted the attention," which might be too absolute.However, the text says it\'s "not given enough attention," implying that some attention is there but insufficient.The problem of children concealing their own situation from their parents is not only well solved, but also given enough attention.Option D suggests "Children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents."This contradicts the text, which implies that the issue is adequately addressed. Therefore, D is not the correct answer.Option A, B, and C are incorrect because they do not align with the information provided in the text.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
