nt. Without such innovation, the assumption that diesel vehicles can reduce emissions and fuel use would not hold, undermining the conclusion. \n\nWhile Option B (\"encourage using diesel cars\") could increase their adoption, it does not address the necessity of ensuring the vehicles themselves are advanced and environmentally friendly. The context specifically highlights \"advanced diesel vehicles,\" making **D** the most critical and specific support for the statement. Options A and C are secondary measures (price incentives or fuel quality) that do not directly drive the technological advancement central to the argument.",
