er other bird flu drugs exist in Vietnam. The focus is on Tamil specifically, not general shortages.  \n- **B** claims \"no medicine for bird flu exists,\" which is incorrect because Tamil exists but is not registered. This is an overstatement.  \n- **C** states it will take time for the drug to circulate widely. Since registration is required and currently lacking, this aligns with the context\u2019s implication that circulation cannot occur until registration is completed.  \n- **D** suggests the Ministry \"should delay registration,\" but the sentence describes the current situation, not a recommendation.  \n\nThe key point is that Tamil\u2019s lack of registration directly causes difficulties in its circulation. This implies delayed or hindered availability until registration occurs, making **C** the correct answer.  \n\n**Answer:** C) It will take some time for bird flu specific drugs to circulate widely in Vietnam.",
