age as the doctor.Hmm, maybe that means Wang is not the doctor?Because if Wang were the doctor, then their age would be the same as the doctor\'s age, which would contradict the clue.Wait, but the clue says "not the same age as the doctor", so if Wang were the doctor, then their age would be the same as the doctor\'s, which is impossible.Therefore, Wang cannot be the doctor.So that leaves Zhang as the doctor?Wait, but let\'s confirm.\n\nWait, if the doctor must be either Wang or Zhang (since Li can\'t be the doctor from clue 3), but clue 2 says that Wang is not the same age as the doctor.If Wang were the doctor, then they would be the same age as themselves, which is impossible, so indeed Wang can\'t be the doctor.Therefore the doctor must be Zhang.Wait, but let\'s see if that holds with the other clues.\n\nWait, if the doctor is Zhang, then according to clue 3, the doctor (Zhang) is younger than Li.So Li is older than Zhang.But from clue 1, Zhang is older than the teacher.So the teacher must be younger than Zhang.So if Zhang is the doctor, then the teacher must be someone younger than Zhang, so either Wang or Li.But Li is older than Zhang, so Li can\'t be the teacher because Zhang is older than the teacher, but Li is older than Zhang.Therefore, the teacher must be Wang.Let\'s see if that works.\n\nSo let\'s suppose:.\n\nDoctor is Zhang.\n\nThen from clue 3, Li > Zhang (in age).\n\nFrom clue 1, Zhang > teacher (so teacher must be Wang, since Li can\'t be the teacher because Li is older than Zhang, but Zhang has to be older than teacher.So teacher is Wang.\n\nSo then professions so far:.\n\nZhang: Doctor.\n\nWang: Teacher.\n\nThen Li must be the lawyer, since the remaining profession is lawyer.\n\nWait, but let\'s check all the clues again with this arrangement.\n\nLet me list the assignments:.\n\nWang: Teacher.\n\nLi: Lawyer.\n\nZhang: Doctor.\n\nNow check the clues:.\n\n1.Zhang is older than the teacher (Wang).Since Zhang is the doctor, and Wang is the teacher, thi