      "text": " D\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is **D) I'm sorry to have caused you trouble because I wasn't serious.**  \n\n### Explanation:  \nDefensive listening involves **denial, defense, or counterattack** to deflect blame. Let\u2019s analyze each option:  \n- **A)** \"You don't work harder than I do\" is a **counterattack**, shifting blame to the accuser (defensive).  \n- **B)** \"You know I always take things seriously\" is a **denial**, rejecting the accusation (defensive).  \n- **C)** \"I haven\u2019t been in good health recently...\" is a **defense**, offering an excuse (defensive).  \n- **D)** \"I'm sorry...\" **acknowledges fault** and apologizes, which is the **opposite** of defensive listening. It accepts responsibility rather than deflecting blame.  \n\nThus, **D** does not belong to defensive listening.  \n\n**Answer:** D",
