messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nAnalogical argument is based on the sameness or similarity of two objects in some attributes, and infers that the two objects are also the same or similar in other attributes. Its logical form is that object A has the attributes of a, b, c and d. Object B has properties of a, b, c. So object B has the property of d.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the followings belongs to analogical argument?\n# Options:\nA) Tao yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, li bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. this shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries\nB) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation\nC) Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, comrade bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that comrade bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others\nD) Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper', "<think>\nOkay, let's see.I need to figure out which of the options A, B, C, or D is an example of an analogical argument based on the definition given..\n\nFirst, the definition says an analogical argument is when two objects (A and B) share some attributes (a, b, c), and then we infer that B also has another attribute (d) that A has.So the structure is: A has a, b, c, d; B has a, b, c; therefore, B has d.\n\nLooking at the options one by one.\n\nOption A: Talks about Tao Yuanming and Li Bai not bowing to authority or wealth, and concludes that ambitious people aren't proud of high salaries.Hmm.This seems to be using two examples to make a general statement about a category (ambitious people).Maybe it's an inductive argument rather than analogical?Because they're both instances leading to a general conclusion.Not sure yet.\n\nOption B: Light and sound both have linear propagation, refraction, reflection.Therefore, since sound has waves, light does too.Oh, this looks like a classic analogy.They share a, b, c (the phenomena listed), so they infer that since sound has waves (d), light does too.That fits the structure exactly.So B might be the answer.\n\nOption C: Comparing Bethune to others who are irresponsible.The argument is that since others are bad in work, Bethune is the opposite, showing he's selfless.Wait, this is more of a contrast rather than a similarity.The shared attributes might be the work attitudes?Or is it contrasting?The conclusion is about his spirit, but the reasoning is based on contrasting traits.Not sure if this fits the analogy structure.\n\nOption D: Silver and copper are both conductive metals, but silver has lower resistivity, so it's better for conductors.Here, the argument is pointing out a difference (resistivity) to conclude one is better.The analogy part would be that since they share being conductive metals (a, b?), but then the conclusion is based on a differing attribute.Maybe an analogical argument because the conclusion is about a difference, inferring a shared attribute.\n\nBreaking it down further. The key is that the argument must infer that B does not have attribute d because A has a,b,c,d and B has a,b,c.\n\nOption B: Light and sound do not share a, b, c (linear, refraction, reflection). Since sound does not have waves (d), then light does not either (d). So that fits perfectly.\n\nOption A is not like two instances leading to a general rule about ambitious people, which is deductive generalization, not analogy between two objects.\n\nOption C is comparing two groups to highlight a trait in one, which might be the same type of reasoning.\n\nOption D does not use a shared attribute (conductivity) but then points out a difference (resistivity) to make a conclusion, so it's inferring a shared attribute and not using a difference.. Therefore, my final option is: "]] 38%|###7      | 226/600 [2:34:38<7:04:53, 68.16s/it]
