      "text": "\uff5c\n\nC) People are exploring new ways to alleviate global warming<\uff5c\n\nWait, hold on. Wait a second, let me recheck. The problem says that improving reflectivity by using light-colored materials, which would increase reflectivity, thereby reducing temperature. The question is about which is correct.\n\nC says \"people are exploring new ways to alleviate global warming\"\u2014yes, because the research is suggesting a method (using light-colored materials on roofs and roads) to reduce global temperature. So that's an attempt to alleviate global warming. So yes, C is correct. The other options have issues. The answer is C. I think that's solid. So the final answer is option C.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{C}\n</think>\n\nThe context discusses new research on improving the reflectivity of urban roofs and roads using light-colored materials to reduce the global average temperature by 0.07\u00b0C. Here's the analysis of each option:\n\n- **Option A**: Incorrect. The passage states the temperature reduction is small (0.07\u00b0C), not \"greatly reduce,\" and does not mention indoor temperature specifically.\n- **Option B**: Incorrect. The passage states that roofs and roads together account for over 60% of the city's surface area, not roads alone being over half.\n- **Option C**: Correct. The research describes a new method (using light-colored materials) to reduce global temperature, indicating people are exploring ways to alleviate global warming.\n- **Option D**: Incorrect. Light-colored materials have higher reflectivity, not dark materials, as stated in the passage.\n\nThe correct answer is **C** because the research highlights an innovative approach to combat global warming.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
