constantly improve the level of social governance\" and \"find a more... just way to protect their rights\". Improving social governance might involve multiple approaches (multi-dimensional, etc.), so D sounds right. The phrase \"from multi-dimensions\" etc. suggests a comprehensive approach to empowering them through various means, which aligns with the passage's emphasis on improving social governance and finding better ways. \n\nTherefore, the answer is D.\n</think>\n\nD) From multi-dimensions, omni-directional, the whole process of empowering the group of migrant workers\n\n**Explanation:**  \nThe passage emphasizes the need to address the rights and well-being of migrant workers through improved social governance and systemic solutions. It highlights the importance of a comprehensive approach (\"constantly improve the level of social governance\"), aiming for a \"more leisurely, safer, more just way\" to protect their rights. Option D aligns with this vision by advocating for empowerment through multi-faceted, holistic measures (\"multi-dimensions, omni-directional, whole process\"). The text does not focus on legal solutions (A), migrant worker participation in governance (B), or the difficulty of the path (C), making D the most fitting choice.",
