messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIntuitive thinking refers to the thinking in which the behavior steps and thinking process are not clear and clear, and some guesses, assumptions or judgments are made directly and quickly about some phenomena or problems.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is typical intuitive thinking?\n# Options:\nA) The public security and criminal police analyzed the case according to the evidence collected\nB) Military commanders make military decisions based on the intelligence materials of the scouts\nC) Solve the problems in the exam based on the knowledge learned\nD) The doctor quickly made a diagnosis of the disease based on the patient's oral materials", '<think>\nOkay, let\'s see.The question is about identifying which option is an example of intuitive thinking as defined here.The definition says intuitive thinking involves unclear steps, guesses, assumptions, or quick judgments without clear processes.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nA) Public security analyzing cases with evidence.That sounds more methodical, using evidence, so maybe not intuitive.\n\nB) Military commanders using scout intelligence.They base decisions on data, so also analytical, not quick guesses?.\n\nC) Solving exam problems with learned knowledge.This isn\'t applying learned methods, unstructured and intuitive.\n\nA) Doctor slowly deliberating over patient\'s info.Hmm, doctors should avoid hasty judgments, particularly if they lack experience, carefully considering all steps before reaching a diagnosis.That goes against the intuitive thinking description because it\'s a deliberate judgment based on thorough analysis with a clear, step-by-step process.\n\nWait, but sometimes doctors disregard protocols.But the key here is "slowly made a diagnosis based on oral materials\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
