which is the best?.\n\nIf the question is about which "best supports", then direct evidence (A) is the strongest..\n\nTherefore, the answer is A. .\n\nWait, but maybe the question is trying to get at the fact that just because plants are in the stomach doesn\'t mean they are an important part of the diet..\n\nWait, the option says "half of their diet was plant."So that\'s 50%, which is a significant portion.So that would support it being an important part..\n\nTherefore, A is correct..\n\nHmm..\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the answer is D. .\n\nWait, maybe the scientists are being doubted because sharks are generally carnivorous, so someone might say "maybe the plants are just accidentally eaten or not digested.".\n\nOption C\'s enzyme shows they can digest plants, so that supports that the plants are a meaningful part of their diet..\n\nOption D\'s nutrient shows they are getting a necessary nutrient from plants, so that\'s important..\n\nSo between C and D, but A is direct..\n\nHmm..\n\nI think I need to make a decision..\nIn this case, option C shows they have an enzyme to digest plants, making the plants a valuable part of their diet... Therefore, my final option is: ']] 54%|#####3    | 322/600 [3:38:51<2:06:09, 27.23s/it]
