t fees for her services.\n\nC) Tanya dutifully represents her clients' best interests.\n\nD) Tanya is bound by extensive ethical codes.\n\nYes, so the last sentence says \"all lawyers are bound...\", so D must be correct.\n\nInitially, I might have confused \"some are not bound\" but that's wrong. The context says \"all are bound\".\n\nSo the correct answer is D.\n</think>\n\nThe context states that \"all lawyers are bound by extensive ethical codes.\" Since Tanya is a lawyer, this universal statement ensures that she must be bound by these codes. \n\n**Analysis of options:**\n- **A**: The text mentions \"some lawyers work in the best interest of the public,\" but this does not imply Tanya specifically works in the public sector.  \n- **B**: Only \"a few unethical\" lawyers charge exorbitant fees, so this cannot be assumed about Tanya.  \n- **C**: While \"nearly all lawyers\" dutifully represent their clients, Tanya could theoretically be among the \"few unethical\" exceptions. Thus, this is not guaranteed.  \n- **D**: The phrase \"all lawyers are bound by extensive ethical codes\" directly applies to Tanya, making this the only statement that **must** be true.  \n\n**Answer:** D) Tanya is bound by extensive ethical codes.",
