      "text": "\uff5c\n\n**Answer:** C) Whether a typical plastic polymer conveyor belt has an approximate serviceable life as least as long as the typical rubber/cotton belt of the same size and shape.\n\n**Explanation:**  \nThe factory aims to minimize costs related to maintenance, repair, and replacement. While plastic belts save energy and have comparable initial costs, their long-term cost-effectiveness depends on their durability. If plastic belts degrade faster than rubber/cotton ones, they would need more frequent replacements, increasing overall expenses. Conversely, if their lifespan is comparable or longer, the energy savings and negligible modification costs make the switch beneficial. Options A, B, and D do not directly address the critical factor of long-term replacement costs, making **C** the most relevant consideration.",
