ational business. To strengthen this claim, we need evidence directly linking international business to higher profits.\n\n**Option A** directly compares Shell to similarly sized oil companies with less international business and shows their lower profits. This comparison isolates international business as a differentiating factor, strongly supporting the stated reason. \n\n**Option B** focuses on oil companies historically being top earners but does not address the role of international business, making it irrelevant to the specific reasoning.\n\n**Option C** suggests other companies are pursuing internationalization, but it does not confirm that Shell\u2019s existing international operations are the cause of its success\u2014it only implies a broader trend.\n\n**Option D** mentions stable oil prices, which could affect all oil companies equally and does not specifically tie Shell\u2019s profits to its international business.\n\nThus, **Option A** most effectively supports the argument by directly demonstrating that international business correlates with higher profits in similar companies.\n\n**Answer: A**",
