erence rather than explicit confirmation of planting. While plausible, it is not the most directly supported option.\n\n- **Option B**: \"During the Spring and Autumn period, rice was not produced in the north.\"  \n  The context states that before the Spring and Autumn period, the north had small amounts of rice planting. It does not mention production during the period itself, making this option incorrect.\n\n- **Option C**: \"Rice was the main food in the Song dynasty.\"  \n  The context explicitly states rice became the main food in the Ming Dynasty, not the Song. Thus, this is incorrect.\n\n- **Option D**: \"Rice has long been one of the five grains in ancient China.\"  \n  The context clearly states that rice was classified as one of the five grains before the Spring and Autumn period. This classification lasted for a long time, making this option directly supported by the text.\n\n### Final Answer\n\\boxed{D}",
