would require four, so it's impossible. Therefore, B cannot be true. So the answer should be B. But the options are A to D. The question is which cannot be true. So yes, B is impossible. Therefore the answer is B.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{B}\n</think>\n\nGiven the problem of assigning seven candidates (F, G, H, I, W, X, Y) to three departments (Public Relations (PR), Production, and Sales) with the specified conditions, we need to determine which statement cannot be true if X and F are in the same department.\n\n### Key Steps:\n1. **Conditions Recap**:\n   - **Condition 1**: H and Y must be in the same department.\n   - **Condition 2**: F and G cannot be in the same department.\n   - **Condition 3**: If X is in Sales, then W must be in Production.\n   - **Condition 4**: F must be in Production.\n\n2. **Given X and F are in the same department**:\n   - Since F must be in Production (Condition 4), X must also be in Production.\n   - Production now has F and X, needing one more member.\n\n3. **Analyzing Each Option**:\n   - **Option A (G in Sales)**:\n     - G cannot be in Production (Condition 2). Assigning G to Sales is possible. \n     - Example assignment: Production (F, X, W), PR (I), Sales (G, H, Y). All conditions satisfied.\n     - **Possible**, so not the answer.\n\n   - **Option B (H in Production)**:\n     - If H is in Production, Y must also be there (Condition 1). \n     - This would require 4 members (F, X, H, Y) in Production, exceeding the limit of 3.\n     - **Impossible**, so this is the answer.\n\n   - **Option C (I in Sales)**:\n     - Example assignment: Production (F, X, W), PR (G), Sales (H, Y, I). All conditions satisfied.\n     - **Possible**, so not the answer.\n\n   - **Option D (W in PR)**:\n     - Example assignment: Production (F, X, I), PR (W), Sales (G, H, Y). All conditions satisfied.\n     - **Possible**, so not the answer.\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe statement that cannot be true is **B**, as placing H in Production would require Y also, exceeding the department's capacity.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
