ings.\n\n**Explanation:**  \nThe argument hinges on the device's ability to effectively locate trapped humans. A key potential weakness is whether the device can distinguish human signals from those of other living beings (e.g., pets, wildlife). Option D directly addresses this concern by stating the device can differentiate human signals, ensuring emergency teams focus on actual survivors. This strengthens the conclusion that the device will improve rescue efforts. Other options either introduce irrelevant details (A), discuss unrelated rescue timelines (B), or present a drawback (C) that weakens the argument. Thus, **D** most effectively bolsters the argument.",
