elike.The passage says it should be "rich and appropriate form" and integrated into life, which might mean making it more real or lifelike."Lifelike" could be a possible fit here.\nThe passage highlights the importance of making history education easily accessible at all times and in all places. The focus is on availability rather than integration and form.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
