      "text": " A is the best choice because it explicitly mentions the social need driving the choice, and he actively sought the qualification. D's social need is less explicit, relying on friends' suggestion and existing experience.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is **A**. \n\n**Analysis:**  \nProfessional socialization involves choosing an occupation based on social needs, acquiring necessary skills, and updating them.  \n\n- **Option A**: Zhang identified a social need (translation talents were urgently needed), actively studied to gain qualifications, and transitioned to the new role. This directly aligns with the definition.  \n- **Option B**: Zhang\u2019s initial assignment in the army was not his own choice based on social needs, so it does not fit.  \n- **Option C**: Li\u2019s motivation was personal interest in cooking, not a recognized social need.  \n- **Option D**: While Chen used experience from raising children, the trigger (friends\u2019 suggestion) and lack of explicit mention of recognizing a social need make it less aligned than A.  \n\nThus, **A** best exemplifies professional socialization as defined.  \n\n**Answer:** A",
      "logprobs": null,
