messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nRural culture is a set of contextual production and life experience system, which is determined by the production and living conditions of the society. in any case, the import of advanced culture from the outside to such a society is divorced from reality.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the most accurate understanding of the meaning of contextual in this paragraph?\n# Options:\nA) Adapted to the experience of production and life in various parts of the countryside\nB) Adapting to the actual development and changes in rural areas\nC) Connected with and integrated with the reality of the local rural society\nD) Adapted to the development of advanced culture', '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out the answer to this question.Let me read through the context again carefully.\n\nThe context says: "Rural culture is a set of contextual production and life experience system, which is determined by the production and living conditions of the society.In any case, the import of advanced culture from the outside to such a society is divorced from reality.".\n\nThe question is asking what "contextual" means here, with options A to D. .\n\nFirst, let\'s break down the sentence where "contextual" is used.The phrase is "contextual production and life experience system."The next sentence talks about importing advanced culture being "divorced from reality," implying that the rural culture is tied to its own reality, not external inputs.\n\nSo the key point is that rural culture is based on its own context, meaning the local conditions.The word "contextual" here likely refers to being connected to the local reality.The second sentence supports this by contrasting imported culture (which is not contextual) with the existing system that is rooted in the society\'s own conditions.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nA) Adapted to the experience of production and life in various parts of the countryside.Hmm, "various parts" might be broader than the local context mentioned.The text emphasizes the society\'s own conditions, so maybe "various parts" is too general?.\n\nB) Adapting to the actual development and changes in rural areas.This mentions adapting to changes, but the original text is more about being determined by existing conditions rather than adapting to changes.Not sure yet.Not connected or integrated with the reality of the local rural society.This seems further. The context suggests that the culture is shaped by factors outside the local society, and importing external culture is good because it\'s not divorced from reality. So "not connected or integrated with local reality" fits.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
