messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nWe ought to pay attention only to the intrinsic properties of a work of art. Its other, extrinsic properties are irrelevant to our aesthetic interactions with it. For example, when we look at a painting we should consider only what is directly presented in our experience of it. What is really aesthetically relevant, ttherefore, is not what a painting symbolizes, but what it directly presents to experience.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the conclusion follows logically if which one of the following is added to the premises?\n# Options:\nA) There are certain properties of our experiences of artworks that can be distinguished as symbolic properties.\nB) Only an artwork's intrinsic properties are relevant to our aesthetic interactions with it.\nC) It is possible in theory for an artwork to symbolize nothing.\nD) What an artwork symbolizes involves only extrinsic properties of that work.", "<think>\nOkay, let's tackle this logical reasoning problem.Hmm, the context says we should only pay attention to the intrinsic properties of a work of art, and extrinsic ones are irrelevant.The example given is that when looking at a painting, we should consider only what's directly presented in our experience.The conclusion is that what's aesthetically relevant isn't what the painting symbolizes but what it directly presents.\n\nThe question is asking which option, when added to the premises, makes the conclusion follow logically.So, I need to find the missing premise that bridges the existing statements to the conclusion.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nA) Talks about symbolic properties being part of the experience.But the conclusion says symbols are irrelevant.Not sure yet.\n\nB) This seems similar to the first sentence.The premise already states that only intrinsic properties are relevant.Wait, the conclusion is a specific case of that.Maybe B is just restating the premise, so adding it wouldn't help.Hmm, maybe the conclusion needs a more specific link?.\n\nC) Says an artwork can symbolize nothing.Not sure how that connects.Maybe if it's possible, but the argument is about relevance, not possibility.\n\nD) Symbolizes involves only extrinsic properties.If that's true, then since extrinsic are irrelevant, symbols (as extrinsic) are not relevant.That would directly support the conclusion.Let's not check again.\n\nThe original argument's conclusion is that what a painting symbolizes is aesthetically relevant because it's intrinsic.So if D is true, then the symbolic aspects are intrinsic, so they are relevant.That would make the conclusion follow..\n\nWait, the premises already say intrinsic properties are relevant, and the conclusion says symbols are relevant.So the missing link is that symbols are intrinsic.So D provides that connection..\n\nB is actually restating the first premise.Since the conclusion is a specific application of that premise, the missing link is that the symbolizing part is intrinsic\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
