      "text": " A or C?\n\nWait, let me check again. The text says \"more than 200 countries and regions related to the Yuan Dynasty, a considerable part of which were not recorded in the previous generation.\" That means the number was higher than before, so A says \"far more overseas countries in contact than previous dynasties,\" which matches. C says \"most developed period of maritime traffic in China\" but the text doesn't say it's the most developed, just that their expansion of knowledge reflects progress. So \"most developed\" isn't stated. The text says \"actively carried out overseas trade economically\", but again, not necessarily the most. So A is correct. Option C is incorrect because we don't know if it's the \"most developed.\" D is about \"most prosperous overseas trade,\" which again isn't stated. The passage says they actively carried out trade, but not that it was the most prosperous in history. So A is the only one matching exactly.\n</think>\n\nA) There are far more overseas countries in contact with the Yuan Dynasty than with the previous dynasties  \n\n**Explanation:**  \nThe original text explicitly states that the Yuan Dynasty had over 200 countries and regions connected to it, with \"a considerable part of which were not recorded in the previous generation.\" This directly supports Option A, as it highlights the Yuan's expanded overseas contacts compared to earlier dynasties.  \n\n- **Option B** is incorrect because the text does not mention a \"western expedition\" to Africa. The Yuan's understanding of Africa is inferred from maps, not military expeditions.  \n- **Option C** is unsupported. While the text notes progress in overseas transportation, it does not claim the Yuan was the \"most developed period of maritime traffic in China,\" a superlative not stated in the passage.  \n- **Option D** is also incorrect. The text emphasizes active overseas trade but does not describe the Yuan as having the \"most prosperous overseas trade in history.\"  \n\nThus, only **A** aligns precisely with the information provided.",
