\n- Thus, LZ received votes from himself and Wang Ming \u2192 full votes (since there are three voters: ZH, WM, LZ).\n\nTherefore, LZ has a full vote, so Li Zilu must not vote for him.\n\nBut Li Zilu, in his own vote, voted for himself because he assumed he didn't have a full vote, but in reality, he did, so he shouldn't have. Contradiction.\n\nThis suggests a paradox, so to avoid it:\n\nPerhaps LZ doesn't vote for himself.\n\nIf LZ votes for ZJ but not himself:\n\nThen, to have a full vote, LZ would need WM's vote, but since LZ didn't vote for himself, he can't have a full vote (needs both WM and himself to vote).\n\nTherefore, he doesn't have a full vote, so Li Zilu (LZ) votes for himself.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- LZ votes for ZJ and himself.\n\n- Wang Ming must vote for all candidates that LZ voted for (ZJ and LZ).\n\n- Thus, Wang Ming votes for ZJ and LZ.\n\n- For LZ's full vote status:\n\n  - Votes for LZ are Wang Ming and LZ himself \u2192 two votes (since ZH didn't vote).\n\n  - Since there are three voters (ZH, WM, LZ), a full vote requires votes from both WM and LZ. Since LZ voted for himself and WM also did, that's two votes, which is a full vote (because all except ZH voted).\n\nTherefore, LZ has a full vote.\n\nThus, Li Zilu (LZ) must not vote for himself because he received a full vote (from WM and himself).\n\nContradiction again.\n\nThis indicates that the only way to avoid contradiction is if LZ doesn't vote for himself and also doesn't get a vote from WM.\n\nLet me try:\n\nScenario where:\n\n- LZ votes for ZJ only (not himself).\n\n- Wang Ming must vote for ZJ and any other candidates that LZ voted for. Since LZ only voted for ZJ, Wang Ming votes for ZJ and possibly others.\n\n- For LZ's full vote status:\n\n  - LZ is a candidate; to have a full vote, he needs votes from WM and himself.\n\n  - Since LZ didn't vote for himself, he can't have a full vote even if WM voted for him.\n\nThus, LZ didn't get a full vote, so Li Zilu (LZ) votes for himself.\n\nBut 