ire quote, there are significant restrictions in practice. The mention of 18 unprotected speech categories in the U.S. and the European Convention\u2019s lengthy restrictions on speech directly supports the idea that **freedom of speech in the West is not absolute**. The focus is on the existence of limitations, not necessarily on hypocrisy or double standards (A), nor on total absence of free speech (B). While the false attribution of the quote (D) is noted, it serves as context to highlight the discrepancy between the West\u2019s rhetoric and reality, not the primary emphasis. Thus, the core message is that Western free speech has boundaries, making **C** the correct answer.",
