ows a logical progression but still explores related concepts, which could be considered divergent.\n- **B) Wave line - wave - sound**: Connects a visual representation (wave line) to physical waves and then to sound waves via analogy. This uses creative association, fitting divergent thinking.\n- **C) Sweater - cotton wool - fiber**: Breaks down the sweater into its material (cotton wool) and then into its components (fiber). This is a **linear, analytical decomposition** of parts to wholes, characteristic of **convergent thinking** rather than divergent.\n- **D) Flowers - children - future**: Uses metaphorical associations (flowers symbolizing growth, children representing the future). This imaginative leap aligns with divergent thinking.\n\n**Conclusion:** Option **C** does not exemplify divergent thinking, as it relies on hierarchical breakdown rather than creative exploration of ideas.\n\n**Answer:** C",
