messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nPeople may be divided into two classes: those who are a little ambitious and those who are not. For ordinary people, a little ambition is a firm motivation to pull them out of their ordinary lives. Without that ambition, can only be powerless and even ignorant, slowly submerged by the ordinary life. In times of change, that bit of ambition can lead to spectacular results.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements constitutes a rebuttal to the above statement?\n# Options:\nA) Liu bei, who made straw sandals, never forgot that he was the emperor's uncle.because of this, he went from empty-handed to one-third of the world.\nB) Although zhang xiong had high ambitions, he was mediocre in intelligence. he worked hard all his life, but nothing was accomplished, and he was bruised and bruised all over.\nC) Liu qin has neither ambition nor special talent, just by virtue of her natural beauty and the help of noble people in her life, she has accomplished many things.\nD) The chrysanthemum elder sister is neither talented nor beautiful, but she thinks highly of herself, constantly toss about, life also lead a prosperous life.", '<think>\nOkay, let\'s see.The problem is asking which of the options A to D rebuts the original statement.The original statement says that people are divided into two classes: those with a little ambition and those without.It claims that a little ambition is a strong motivator for ordinary people to rise above their ordinary lives.Without that ambition, people become powerless and ignorant, getting submerged by ordinary life.And in times of change, that ambition leads to spectacular results.\n\nSo, a rebuttal would be a statement that contradicts this argument.The argument\'s main points are that a little ambition is necessary to succeed, and without it, you fail.Also, that ambition leads to success, especially in changing times.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nOption A: Liu Bei made straw sandals but never forgot he was the emperor\'s uncle.Because of this, he went from nothing to controlling a third of the world.This seems to support the original argument because it\'s an example of someone with ambition (remembering his status) leading to success.So A is not a rebuttal.\n\nOption B: Zhang Xiong had high ambitions but was mediocre in intelligence.He worked hard all his life but achieved nothing and got bruised.Hmm, this might be a rebuttal because here someone with ambition (maybe more than "a little") didn\'t succeed.The original says "a little ambition" is good, but if having high ambition doesn\'t lead to success, maybe that challenges the idea that ambition (even a little) leads to success.But the original says "a little" is enough.So if someone has too much ambition (high) and fails, maybe that\'s not a direct rebuttal.Wait, the original says "a little ambition is a firm motivation..Without that ambition, you fail."So the rebuttal would be someone with ambition who still fails, or someone without ambition who succeeds?Let me check again.\n\nThe original says that without ambition, you can\'t escape ordinary life.So if someone has ambition and still fails, that could question the necessity of ambition leading to success.But the argument says "a little ambition is a firm motivation to pull them out of their ordinary lives."So maybe the key is that a little is sufficient, but if someone with ambition (maybe a lot) fails, maybe that\'s not a direct counter.Or maybe the original\'s point is that ambition is needed, but this example shows that even with ambition, if you lack other qualities (like intelligence), you can fail.So maybe that\'s a rebuttal because it shows ambition alone isn\'t enough.The original might be oversimplifying by saying ambition is sufficient, but B shows that other factors matter.So B could be a rebuttal.\n\nOption C: Liu Qin has no ambition or special talent, but through natural beauty and help from nobles, she achieved things.This directly contradicts the original statement\'s claim that without ambition, you can\'t achieve anything.Here\'s someone without ambition who still succeeded.So this would be a strong rebuttal because the original says without ambition you can\'t get out of ordinary life, but here\'s someone who didn\'t have ambition but succeeded.So C is a good candidate.\n\nOption D: Chrysanthemum sister isn\'t talented or beautiful, but she\'s arrogant and restless, leading a prosperous life.Wait, "thinks highly of herself" might be similar to ambition?Or arrogance?The original says "a little ambition" is good.If she\'s "constantly toss about" (maybe restless or active) and that leads to success, but she has self-esteem.Maybe this is an example of someone with some form of ambition (arrogance as a form of overconfidence?)leading to success.Or maybe the "toss about" is like ambition.If she\'s not ambitious but still succeeds, but the description says she "thinks highly of herself," which could be a form of ambition.Alternatively, maybe the key is that she has no talent or beauty but still succeeded, but through her own actions.The original says without ambition you can\'t, but if she has some ambition (even if not a little?), but the question is whether her case contradicts.Hmm, the original says those without ambition can\'t succeed, but D\'s case: she\'s not talented or beautiful but has self-esteem and is restless.If "thinks highly of herself" is a form of ambition, then maybe that\'s the ambition part.Then it\'s supporting the original.But if she has no ambition but still succeeded through other means, then it\'s a rebuttal.The problem is the exact wording.The original\'s two classes are those with a little ambition and those without.If she has some ambition (even high?), but the original says even a little is enough.Conversely, perhaps the "thinks highly of herself" is indeed ambition rather than arrogance.The original\'s argument emphasizes the necessity of a significant amount of ambition.If D\'s situation is someone lacking ambition (since she is not in the first class) yet still achieved success, then that supports the argument.But the description indicates she "thinks highly of herself" and "constantly toss about," suggesting she possesses considerable ambition.So perhaps D is not a counterargument..\n\nSo the choice is between B and C. Let me summarize the original argument:.\n\nPremise: Individuals can be categorized into two groups: those with a substantial amount of ambition (class 1) and those without (class 2)..\n\nConclusion: Lack of ambition (class 2) traps individuals in an ordinary existence, whereas possessing a significant amount of ambition (class 1) enables success, particularly during times of change.\n\nA counterargument would demonstrate that either an individual in class 2 (lacking ambition) achieved success, or an individual in class 1 (ambitious) failed..\n\nOption C represents an individual in class 2 (lacking ambition) who achieved success (accomplished numerous feats through beauty and noble assistance).This directly challenges the assertion that individuals in class 2 cannot succeed.Therefore, C serves as a clear counterargument.\n\nOption B represents an individual in class 1 (ambitious) who failed.This contradicts the notion that ambition leads to success.However, the original statement suggests that "a little ambition is a strong motivator" — perhaps the issue with B is that the individual had "excessive ambitions" (too much?), rather than "a little."The original specifies that "a little ambition" is the sufficient amount.So if Zhang possessed high ambitions (more than a little), then his failure may not contradict the original argument, which asserts that a little is ample.So B may not effectively counter the original argument as it concerns an individual with more than a little ambition.The original does not claim that greater ambition is superior, only that a little is adequate.So B\'s failure could be attributed to other factors, indicating that the original statement about the adequacy of a little ambition remains unchallenged.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 99%|#########9| 594/600 [6:14:07<04:23, 43.94s/it]
